[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Saber is installed. Two things need doing before it is useful.

1. Start it with your session. Saber is resident, not invoked, so it belongs in
   the compositor's autostart rather than on a key binding:

     echo 'saber &' >> ~/.config/hikari/autostart
     chmod +x ~/.config/hikari/autostart

   Starting it there rather than later also removes a caveat the old
   arrangement had: a tray application asks exactly once, at its own startup,
   whether a tray host exists, and one that finds none shows no icon and never
   asks again. A panel that is already running when your session starts is
   never the process that arrives too late.

2. Join the operator group, if you want the session controls.

   Suspend, reboot and shut down run as you. Saber installs nothing setuid or
   setgid and writes no sudoers rule -- FreeBSD already ships the group for
   this, and /sbin/shutdown and /dev/acpi are already set up for it:

     pw groupmod operator -m <user>

   The change takes effect at the user's next login. Without it Saber simply
   HIDES those three entries rather than offering buttons that fail, so
   declining this is a supported configuration and not a broken one.

DO NOT run "sofi -tray-daemon" alongside Saber. Exactly one process on a
session bus can own org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher, so the two tray hosts
cannot coexist -- you get whichever registered first, and applications that
started before it show no icon at all. Remove it from your autostart, or
rebuild this port with the TRAY option off to keep using it instead.

Everything else about sofi is unaffected: its application menu, notification
daemon and notification history are not superseded, and neither is the
compositor's own top bar, which keeps all system telemetry.

Saber has no theme file. It reads ui { palette } out of your hikari.conf, so
retheming the compositor retints the panel with it. Configuration, all of it
optional, is ~/.config/saber/saber.conf in the same UCL syntax.
EOM
}
{ type: remove
  message: <<EOM
Saber is removed, but two references to it may remain.

Remove the "saber" line from ~/.config/hikari/autostart, or the session will
report a missing binary on every start.

If you disabled "sofi -tray-daemon" when you installed Saber, re-enable it now
or your session will have no system tray at all. Restart the applications whose
tray icons you want afterwards: a tray application asks for a host only once, at
its own startup.

Group membership is left alone. If you added a user to the operator group for
Saber's session controls and want that reverted:

     pw groupmod operator -d <user>
EOM
}
]
